Package: SIEVER
Title: Scale Item Evaluation and Validation Environment
Version: 0.9.0
Date: 2026-11-20
Authors@R: person("Ken", "Kelley", email = "kkelley@nd.edu",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4756-8360"))
Description: An interactive environment for developing constructs and instruments,
    evaluating score interpretations and intended uses, and retaining the
    evidence and researcher decisions behind them. The 'shiny' application
    connects item and facet assignments, screening, exploratory and
    confirmatory factor analysis, reliability with confidence intervals,
    validity-related analyses, scoring, and internal evaluation. Project
    files preserve data, transformations, specifications, and decision
    records. Optional local guidance and review briefs support scientific
    judgment. Estimation is delegated to 'DMAR', 'lavaan', and 'psych';
    favorable coefficients or model fit do not by themselves establish
    validity. Reliability coefficients are reported with confidence
    intervals following Kelley and Pornprasertmanit (2016)
    <doi:10.1037/a0040086>. Sample size planning for narrow confidence
    intervals follows accuracy in parameter estimation, reviewed by
    Maxwell, Kelley, and Rausch (2008)
    <doi:10.1146/annurev.psych.59.103006.093735>, with the root mean square
    error of approximation planned as in Kelley and Lai (2011)
    <doi:10.1080/00273171.2011.543027>. Latent variable models are fit
    with 'lavaan', described by Rosseel (2012) <doi:10.18637/jss.v048.i02>.
